comment.body:
Thanks for the report. Because one monitor is detected and the Samsung is not, we still need to narrow this to either monitor discovery, the connection path, or DDC/CI capability probing. Could you please provide:
1. the full monitor topology (how each display is connected: GPU/port, dock/KVM/adaptor, and cable type), plus whether DDC/CI is enabled in the Samsung monitor OSD;
2. whether the Samsung is visible in Windows Display Settings and Device Manager at the same time Power Display misses it;
3. whether reconnecting the Samsung or toggling increased compatibility changes the result at all; and
4. a fresh diagnostic bundle captured immediately after reproducing by commenting /bugreport on the issue and attaching the generated ZIP.
That will let us tell whether this is a discovery problem or a narrower monitor-capability path.
